Feature: The values of the contract
  The rules of the answers, the events and the refusals, checked on values.

  Scenario: A refusal invalid_request carries its own code
    When I check an "invalid_request" with:
      | error_code  | error_message |
      | UNKNOWN_SKU | No            |
    Then the value is rejected by "code_is" of "invalid_request"

  Scenario: A refusal invalid_request carries a message
    When I check an "invalid_request" with:
      | error_code      |
      | INVALID_REQUEST |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "invalid_request"

  Scenario: A refusal unknown_sku carries its own code
    When I check an "unknown_sku" with:
      | error_code       | error_message | sku      |
      | UNKNOWN_LOCATION | No            | WIDGET-1 |
    Then the value is rejected by "code_is" of "unknown_sku"

  Scenario: A refusal unknown_sku carries a message
    When I check an "unknown_sku" with:
      | error_code  | sku      |
      | UNKNOWN_SKU | WIDGET-1 |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "unknown_sku"

  Scenario: A refusal unknown_location carries its own code
    When I check an "unknown_location" with:
      | error_code  | error_message | location   |
      | UNKNOWN_SKU | No            | AMS-B-0142 |
    Then the value is rejected by "code_is" of "unknown_location"

  Scenario: A refusal unknown_location carries a message
    When I check an "unknown_location" with:
      | error_code       | location   |
      | UNKNOWN_LOCATION | AMS-B-0142 |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "unknown_location"

  Scenario: A refusal insufficient_stock carries its own code
    When I check an "insufficient_stock" with:
      | error_code  | error_message | short_lines                                                                         |
      | UNKNOWN_SKU | No            | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "requested": 401, "available": 400}] |
    Then the value is rejected by "code_is" of "insufficient_stock"

  Scenario: A refusal insufficient_stock carries a message
    When I check an "insufficient_stock" with:
      | error_code         | short_lines                                                                         |
      | INSUFFICIENT_STOCK | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "requested": 401, "available": 400}] |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "insufficient_stock"

  Scenario: A refusal reservation_not_found carries its own code
    When I check a "reservation_not_found" with:
      | error_code  | error_message | reservation_id                       |
      | UNKNOWN_SKU | No            | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 |
    Then the value is rejected by "code_is" of "reservation_not_found"

  Scenario: A refusal reservation_not_found carries a message
    When I check a "reservation_not_found" with:
      | error_code            | reservation_id                       |
      | RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "reservation_not_found"

  Scenario: A refusal invalid_state carries its own code
    When I check an "invalid_state" with:
      | error_code  | error_message | reservation_id                       | state   |
      | UNKNOWN_SKU | No            | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 | SHIPPED |
    Then the value is rejected by "code_is" of "invalid_state"

  Scenario: A refusal invalid_state carries a message
    When I check an "invalid_state" with:
      | error_code    | reservation_id                       | state   |
      | INVALID_STATE | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 | SHIPPED |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "invalid_state"

  Scenario: A refusal open_reservation_exists carries its own code
    When I check an "open_reservation_exists" with:
      | error_code  | error_message | order_id |
      | UNKNOWN_SKU | No            | ORD-1    |
    Then the value is rejected by "code_is" of "open_reservation_exists"

  Scenario: A refusal open_reservation_exists carries a message
    When I check an "open_reservation_exists" with:
      | error_code      | order_id |
      | INVALID_REQUEST | ORD-1    |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "open_reservation_exists"

  Scenario: A refusal forbidden carries its own code
    When I check a "forbidden" with:
      | error_code  | error_message | role  |
      | UNKNOWN_SKU | No            | clock |
    Then the value is rejected by "code_is" of "forbidden"

  Scenario: A refusal forbidden carries a message
    When I check a "forbidden" with:
      | error_code | role  |
      | FORBIDDEN  | clock |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "forbidden"

  Scenario: A refusal idempotency_conflict carries its own code
    When I check an "idempotency_conflict" with:
      | error_code  | error_message | idempotency_key |
      | UNKNOWN_SKU | No            | reserve-0001    |
    Then the value is rejected by "code_is" of "idempotency_conflict"

  Scenario: A refusal idempotency_conflict carries a message
    When I check an "idempotency_conflict" with:
      | error_code           | idempotency_key |
      | IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT | reserve-0001    |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "idempotency_conflict"

  Scenario Outline: A refusal with a wrong code or message is rejected
    When I check an "unknown_sku" with:
      | error_code   | error_message   | sku      |
      | <error_code> | <error_message> | WIDGET-1 |
    Then the value is rejected by "<rule>" of "<definition>"

    Examples:
      | rule      | definition    | error_code  | error_message |
      | enum      | error_code    | NOT_FOUND   | No            |
      | minLength | error_message | UNKNOWN_SKU | ""            |

  Scenario Outline: A short line that breaks a rule is rejected
    When I check an "insufficient_stock" with:
      | error_code         | error_message | short_lines   |
      | INSUFFICIENT_STOCK | No            | <short_lines> |
    Then the value is rejected by "<rule>" of "<definition>"

    Examples:
      | rule     | definition  | short_lines                                                     |
      | minItems | short_lines | []                                                              |
      | required | short_line  | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "requested": 5}] |

  Scenario Outline: A stock level that breaks a rule is rejected
    When I check a "stock_level" with:
      | sku      | location   | on_hand   | reserved   | available   |
      | WIDGET-1 | AMS-B-0142 | <on_hand> | <reserved> | <available> |
    Then the value is rejected by "<rule>" of "<definition>"

    Examples:
      | rule                                | definition  | on_hand | reserved | available |
      | minimum                             | on_hand     | -1      | 0        | 0         |
      | minimum                             | reserved    | 10      | -1       | 11        |
      | minimum                             | available   | 10      | 11       | -1        |
      | available_is_on_hand_minus_reserved | stock_level | 10      | 4        | 5         |
      | required                            | stock_level | 10      | 4        |           |

  Scenario Outline: An event that breaks a rule is rejected
    When I check a "stock_event" with:
      | event_id   | event_type   | sku      | location   | quantity_changed | level                                                                                            | occurred_at              |
      | <event_id> | <event_type> | WIDGET-1 | <location> | -5               | {"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 495, "reserved": 100, "available": 395} | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z |
    Then the value is rejected by "<rule>" of "<definition>"

    Examples:
      | rule                    | definition  | event_id                             | event_type    | location   |
      | pattern                 | event_id    | event-1                              | StockAdjusted | AMS-B-0142 |
      | enum                    | event_type  | 7d3f1c2a-5b4e-4a6d-9c8b-000000000001 | StockMoved    | AMS-B-0142 |
      | level_is_the_event_pair | stock_event | 7d3f1c2a-5b4e-4a6d-9c8b-000000000001 | StockAdjusted | AMS-B-0143 |
      | required                | stock_event |                                      | StockAdjusted | AMS-B-0142 |

  Scenario: An event with all its values is accepted
    When I check a "stock_event" with:
      | event_id                             | event_type    | sku      | location   | quantity_changed | level                                                                                            | occurred_at              | reason  |
      | 7d3f1c2a-5b4e-4a6d-9c8b-000000000001 | StockAdjusted | WIDGET-1 | AMS-B-0142 | -5               | {"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 495, "reserved": 100, "available": 395} | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | DAMAGED |
    Then the value is accepted

  Scenario: A StockDepleted event needs its time
    When I check a "stock_depleted" with:
      | event_id                             | sku      | location   |
      | 7d3f1c2a-5b4e-4a6d-9c8b-000000000001 | WIDGET-1 | AMS-B-0142 |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "stock_depleted"

